RA ISAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KISHIMA KOICHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OSATO KIYOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ICHIMURA, ISAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KISHIMA, KOICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OSATO, KIYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An optical head (1) which mounts thereon an optical means for converging a laser beam to be applied to an optical recording medium (51) and which is formed by providing therein an objective lens (2) for converging a laser beam (L), a solid immersion lens (3) interposed between the objective lens (2) and the optical recording medium (51), a holding member (4) for integrally holding the lenses (2, 3) and a moving mechanism (5a) for moving the holding member (4) in the optical axis directions of the lenses (2, 3), a surface facing the optical recording medium (51) consisting of a conductive material, whereby it is possible to increase a numerical aperture by the solid immersion lens (3), control with a high accuracy an air gap based on a capacitance formed between the conductive material and the recording medium (51), and further simplify the moving mechanism (5a) for a focusing servo and signal processing.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un tête optique (1) sur laquelle sont montés des moyens optiques destinés à focaliser un faisceau laser destiné à être appliqué sur un support (51) d'enregistrement optique. Cette tête optique comprend un objectif (2) destiné à faire converger le faisceau laser (L); une lentille (3) à immersion solide interposée entre l'objectif (2) et le support (51) d'enregistrement optique; un élément (4) de support destiné au support intégral des lentilles (2, 3) et un mécanisme (5a) de déplacement servant à déplacer l'élément (4) de support dans le sens de l'axe optique des lentilles (2, 3); et une surface, constituée d'un matériau conducteur, faisant face au support (51) d'enregistrement optique, ce qui permet d'obtenir une ouverture numérique plus grande au moyen de la lentille (3) à immersion solide, de commander avec une grande précision l'entrefer en fonction de la capacité formée entre le matériau conducteur et le support (51) d'enregistrement, et de simplifier, en outre, le mécanisme (5a) de déplacement du servomécanisme de focalisation et le traitement du signal.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>